# DXIL containers written by the probe chain and by measure.py: the library, the linked
# shader, and the directly-compiled controls. All derived -- `python .../triage.py run
# --issue 4168` and `python measure.py` recreate them, and the readable result (what
# `dxa -dumpreflection` said about each) is what is committed, in out-*.txt and variant-*.txt.
# A committed .dxo would also be a stale copy waiting to be mistaken for evidence.
*.dxo

# check-dxl-equivalence.py builds its four containers here and recreates the directory itself,
# so nothing depends on git storing it. The sha256 comparison it draws from them is committed
# in manual-case-dxl-equivalence.txt.
scratch-dxl-equiv/
